<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">High Priest of Amun</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The High Priest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amun">Amun</a> was the chief priest of the god Amun at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thebes">Thebes</a>, controlling the god's vast temple estates. As royal power weakened in the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/twentieth-dynasty-of-egypt">Twentieth Dynasty</a>, the high priests became a rival authority to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaoh</a>. By around 1100 BCE they effectively ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-egypt">Upper Egypt</a>, marking the end of the Egyptian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a>.</p></div>
